    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 16,
    "summary": "Samson carries away the doors of the gate of Gaza—He loves Delilah, who delivers him to the Philistines—He destroys a building, killing himself and 3,000 others.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then went Samson to Gaza, and saw there an harlot, and went in unto her.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 16:1",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it was told the Gazites, saying, Samson is come hither. And they compassed him in, and laid wait for him all night in the gate of the city, and were quiet all the night, saying, In the morning, when it is day, we shall kill him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "Josh. 6:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Josh. 6:3.",
            "prettyString": "Joshua 6:3",
            "references": [
              {
