        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 16:5",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Delilah said to Samson, Tell me, I pray thee, wherein thy great strength lieth, and wherewith thou mightest be bound to afflict thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 16:6",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And Samson said unto her, If they bind me with seven green withs that were never dried, then shall I be weak, and be as another man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "OR new cords; e.g., fresh or moist sinews from animals."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 16:7",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the lords of the Philistines brought up to her seven green withs which had not been dried, and she bound him with them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 16:8",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Now there were men lying in wait, abiding with her in the chamber. And she said unto him, The Philistines be upon thee, Samson. And he brake the withs, as a thread of tow is broken when it toucheth the fire. So his strength was not known.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 108
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 16:9",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 16,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And Delilah said unto Samson, Behold, thou hast mocked me, and told me lies: now tell me, I pray thee, wherewith thou mightest be bound.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Mocking."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Mocking.",
            "prettyString": "TG Mocking",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
